# Authenticating AI agents with Netlify

How an AI agent gets credentials to act on a Netlify account. Every method ends with a bearer token that acts as a Netlify user. A human always grants access, either by approving an OAuth prompt or by creating a token. There is no anonymous or agent-only credential.

## Discover

- **MCP server (recommended for agents):** `https://netlify-mcp.netlify.app/mcp` (Streamable HTTP). Its OAuth details are published as RFC 9728 protected-resource metadata at `https://netlify-mcp.netlify.app/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` and RFC 8414 authorization-server metadata at `https://netlify-mcp.netlify.app/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`.
- **REST API:** `https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/`, described by the OpenAPI spec at `https://open-api.netlify.com/swagger.json`.
- **Catalog:** `https://www.netlify.com/.well-known/ard.json` lists the MCP server card, the OpenAPI spec, and Netlify's agent skills.

## Pick a method

### 1. Connect through the MCP server (OAuth 2.1)

Use this for agents and AI clients that speak MCP. No token handling is needed by the user.

1. Call the MCP endpoint without a token. It responds `401` with a `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="…"` header pointing at the protected-resource metadata.
2. Read `authorization_servers` from that document, then fetch the authorization-server metadata.
3. Register your client dynamically at the `registration_endpoint` (RFC 7591). Public clients use `token_endpoint_auth_method: none`.
4. Send the user to the `authorization_endpoint` with the authorization-code flow and PKCE (`code_challenge_method=S256` is required). The user signs in and approves access on app.netlify.com.
5. Exchange the code at the `token_endpoint`. Request the `offline_access` scope if you need a refresh token (`grant_type=refresh_token`).

Most MCP clients do all of this automatically when you add the server URL. For example: `npx -y add-mcp https://netlify-mcp.netlify.app/mcp`.

### 2. Use a personal access token (scripts, CI, local tools)

1. In the Netlify UI, open **User settings > Applications > Personal access tokens** (`https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens`) and select **New access token**.
2. Name it, pick an expiration date, and, if your team uses SAML SSO, choose whether to allow access to that team.
3. Copy the token when it's shown. It can't be viewed again.

A personal access token works against the REST API, as `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` for the Netlify CLI, and as `NETLIFY_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` for the local MCP server (`npx -y @netlify/mcp`). The hosted MCP server also accepts one directly as its bearer token.

### 3. Build a public integration (OAuth2 app)

If other people will authorize your application, you must use OAuth2 rather than asking users for tokens. Register an OAuth application at `https://app.netlify.com/applications` to get a client ID and secret. Send users to `https://app.netlify.com/authorize`, then exchange the authorization code at `https://api.netlify.com/oauth/token`.

### 4. Use the Netlify CLI

Run `netlify login`. It opens a browser for the user to authorize **Netlify CLI** and stores the token in the CLI's global `config.json`. In CI or other non-interactive environments, set `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` to a personal access token instead.

## Use the access token

Send the token as a bearer token over HTTPS:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN" \
     -H "User-Agent: MyAgent (you@example.com)" \
     https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/sites
```

The REST API allows up to 500 requests per minute for most requests, and deploys are limited to 3 per minute and 100 per day. The `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset` response headers report your current status.

## Errors

- **REST API:** a missing, invalid, or revoked token returns `401` with the JSON body `{"code":401,"message":"Access Denied"}`. Get a new token; don't retry with the same one.
- **MCP server:** returns `401` with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="MCP Server", resource_metadata="https://netlify-mcp.netlify.app/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp"`. An expired or invalid token also carries `error="invalid_token"`. Restart the OAuth flow, or use your refresh token.
- **SAML SSO teams:** personal access tokens are denied access to an SSO team unless access was granted when the token was created.

## Revocation

Manage all grants at `https://app.netlify.com/user/applications`:

- **OAuth grants** (the MCP server, Netlify CLI, third-party apps) are listed under **Authorized applications**. Choose **Options > Revoke access**.
- **Personal access tokens** are listed under **Personal access tokens**. Choose **Options > Delete personal token**.

Resetting your Netlify password permanently invalidates every personal access token and OAuth token created before the reset.

